      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Tiny holes on your tomato leaves, even without visible bugs, are often the work of tiny, unseen pests, like thrips or spider mites. These minuscule creatures can be incredibly damaging, causing leaf damage that looks like tiny punctures or holes. It's a good idea to inspect the undersides of the leaves, as that's where many of these little pests like to hide, even if they aren't actively crawling when you look. Treating them early is key to saving your harvest!",
