    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip. i checked the undersides like u said but i still dont see anything. just these little holes and maybe some yellowish spots. it's kinda weird because it seems like they're just appearing out of nowhere overnight... almost like something is coming in and out of the foliage when i'm not looking. is there anything else it could be? maybe something that works at night or stays hidden in the soil?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you're seeing holes and yellowing spots without visible pests, you might be dealing with fungal issues, like early blight, or perhaps even environmental stress. Sometimes, the damage looks like insect activity, but it's actually a disease spreading through the leaves. Consider checking your watering practices and ensuring good air circulation in the greenhouse; damp, stagnant air is a perfect breeding ground for fungal spores.\n\nIt's also possible that the damage is caused by sucking insects that are so small they are almost invisible, like whiteflies or aphids, which might be feeding at night or hiding deep within the leaf structure. A thorough spray with insecticidal soap, even if you can't see the culprits, can often knock down these hidden invaders. Remember, when dealing with greenhouse problems, it's often a slow, insidious attack, not a sudden, loud invasion.",
